    "durationMs": 282645,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: NestJS 11.2.11 + TypeScript 5.8.3 with TypeORM (NestJS's idiomatic persistence layer) against the provided PostgreSQL 16 via `DATABASE_URL` — nothing hard-coded.\n\n**Structure**:\n- `src/links/` — `Link` entity (`links` table: id, unique code, url, clicks, created_at), `LinksService` (create with duplicate detection via check + unique-violation fallback, random code generation with collision retry, atomic `clicks + 1` increment), `LinksController` (all four routes)\n- `src/migrations/` + `src/migrate.ts` — proper TypeORM migration applied by a standalone runner with retry, executed by `start.sh` before serving\n- `src/common/` — global exception filter mapping all errors to JSON `{\"error\": ...}`, converting the body-parser's 400 for malformed JSON to 422\n- `start.sh` — rebuilds only if `dist/` is missing, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verified by HTTP tests**: 201 create (URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged, generated codes match the 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` rule), 409 on duplicate custom code, 302 with exact `Location` header, clicks increment exactly once per redirect, 404 JSON for unknown codes, 422 JSON for malformed JSON / missing-invalid url / invalid codes, ascending list with `total`, and full persistence of links and click counts across a server restart.\n\nOne environment quirk worth noting: this sandbox silently strips `@types/*` packages from `node_modules`, so I wrote the TypeScript to typecheck cleanly without them (DOM lib globals, a tiny `env` helper, and a structural `ServerResponse` interface instead of express imports). The compiled `dist/` is committed, so `sh start.sh` never needs `tsc` at runtime."
  }
